    "content": "![](assets/7a9b97e711c726af17.png)\n\n\n\n**View:** \\[PA and Lateral / AP Portable\\] Chest X-ray\n**Findings:**\n- There is **blunting of the right costophrenic angle**, consistent with a **moderate right pleural effusion**.\n- **Meniscus sign** is present, indicating fluid layering in the right pleural space.\n- The right hemidiaphragm is **partially obscured**.\n- There is a **mild shift of the mediastinum to the left**, suggesting volume effect from the effusion.\n- The underlying lung fields on the right are **partially obscured**, but no obvious consolidation or mass is seen.\n- The left lung appears **clear**, and the left costophrenic angle is **sharp**.\n- Cardiac silhouette is **within normal limits**.\n- No evidence of pneumothorax or acute bony abnormalities.\n**Impression:**\n- **Right-sided pleural effusion**, moderate in volume."
