    "category": "orders",
    "status": "released",
    "content": "<table><tr><td>Time / Shift</td><td>Provider order</td><td>Provider</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Admit to labor and deliver for postpartum care</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Full code</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Regular diet</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td><span discussion-urls=\"discussion://333195d2-01d5-8077-a3c8-001cabdcee5d\">Activity: Patient may get up to bathroom once recovery is complete .Nurse should assist patient with first time up out of bed. </span></td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>LR 1000ml to infuse at 125ml/hr, may saline lock IV 3 hours after delivery if bleeding is scant.</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Vital signs: every 15 mins x 4 for 1st hour after delivery, then q 30 mins x2 for 2nd hour. Then q 8 hours until discharge. Fundal messages and lochia assessment to be done with vital signs.</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Lab: CBC post delivery and the first am after delivery</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>I & O q shift</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Pitocin 30 units added to 500ml Normal Saline to infuse at 334 ml/hr. after delivery of placenta for for 100 mls then decrease rate to 95mls per hour until bag is complete.  May saline lock IV 3 hours after delivery if bleeding is scant.</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Witch hazel pads applied to hemorrhoids prn</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Epifoam spray to perineum as needed for pain</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Percocet  1 tab po for C/O pain every 4 hours</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Ibuprofen 600mg po q 6 hours as needed for pain</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td>Today</td><td>Weigh all pads for the first 2 hours after delivery.</td><td>Dr. Nelson</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>**If hemorrhage is suspected, call MD with assessment findings and bleeding amounts for specific medication orders. These are the medications you should expect.**<br>  1. **Methylergonovine (Methergine)**0.2 mg IM every 2–4 hours as needed.<br>  2. **Carboprost (Hemabate)**250 mcg IM every 15–90 minutes as needed; maximum approximately 2 mg total.**Specific MD/provider order required before administration.**<br>  3. **Misoprostol**600–1000 mcg PR / SL / PO as needed per protocol. **Specific MD/provider order required before administration.**<br>  4. **Tranexamic Acid (TXA) **1 g IV over 10 minutes once postpartum hemorrhage is diagnosed. May repeat 1 g after 30 minutes–24 hours if bleeding persists, per protocol.<br>**Specific MD/provider order required before administration.**</td><td>Dr Darnell</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>cbc in 6 hrs</td><td>Dr. Darnell/KR</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>foley cath</td><td>Dr. Darnell/KR</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>15 min fundus  checks</td><td>Dr. Darnell/KR</td></tr></table>"
