    "content": "Jane Fowler \n<table><tr><td>Time / Shift</td><td>Provider order</td><td>Provider</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Admit to PACU for recovery of Hysterectomy with bilateral salpingo-opherectomy</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Vital signs q 5 mins for first 30 mins, then q 15 mins x 1 hours</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Diet: Sips of H2O, advance to clear liquids as tolerated</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Maintain pulse ox above 95%, titrate O2 as needed</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>If issues with sedation during recovery notify anesthesia</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Activity: Bedrest now, out of bed tonight</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>IV: LR @125ml/hr</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>INPUT AND OUTPUT Q4 hours. Call MD if urine output is less than 30ml per hour.</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Bilateral SCD’s</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Morphine 2 mg IV push every 4 hours as needed for pain; may repeat/titrate to a maximum of 10 mg per dose, not to exceed more that 10mg every 4 hours.</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Zofran 4mg IVP q 4 hours prn nausea/vomiting</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Consult oncologist when patient gets to surgical floor</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>Transfer to surgical floor after 1 hour recover.</td><td>Dr. Smith MD</td></tr></table>"
